<%#
  Rendered into the session card by the dashboard.

  The binding here is the BatchConnect::Session, so user_context is available --
  the launch form values, read back from user_defined_context.json. That is a
  different binding from view.html.erb, which sees only the connection info and
  the keys of <pod>-secret.

  Keys are form attribute ids, so this tracks form.yml's `working_dir`.

  Shown only when the user set one. "Working directory: your home" on every
  default session is noise, and its absence is not ambiguous once the card is
  known to call out a non-default choice and stay quiet otherwise -- which is how
  the other CIRRUS apps read.
-%>
<%- workdir = user_context["working_dir"].to_s.strip -%>
<%- unless workdir.empty? -%>
**Opens in:** `<%= workdir %>`
<%- end -%>

R packages you install go to `~/rstudio/r-libs/`, and your RStudio settings to
`~/rstudio/config/`. Neither is the library or the configuration your Casper and
Derecho sessions use — packages built in this container will not load there.
